s. Chi-ing T7 to get a Chow uses T8 and T9, which are terminals, so it could help with Outside Hand or Terminal patterns. But overall, the hand is weak, and discarding later might be better.\n\nReason: I recommend Pass because it's too early to expose your hand; you have no clear direction, and preserving flexibility is important. Chi-ing would commit you to a Bamboo sequence and reveal part of your hand, potentially helping opponents. Also, you have two pairs (F2 and J2) that could become pungs, and other tiles like W2-W3 could form a Chow if you draw W1 or W4. Passing allows you to draw a new tile and reassess.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
